It's one of many forms of remote/missile combat.  Throwing almost
anything, zapping any wand that will not destroy the boulder, and
so on.  It also works just fine to throw artifact super-weapons, then
push the boulder over them burying them.  Rocks are rather less
expensive than artifact weapons, though.  Sokoban in particular is
a level where you want missiles so cheap they aren't worth digging
a pit to retrieve them, and that's rocks.

Remote combat beats melee combat by such a large margin it
doesn't leave a pit, it leaves an entire destroyed dungeon level.
You see, monsters attacked with missile weapons can not hit you
with their melee weapons.  sure, they can throw their own missiles
but few come equiped with enough to kill you but you're smart
enough to pick up lots of missiles once you learn the value of
missile combat.


